1. The rule in holes() against a plain scan in reading order, and against 'the blocks that were empty before the deletion'
   orders 2 to 60: equal to the plain scan at every step: True; orders 2 to 200: equal to the blocks empty before the deletion: True; holes = order + deleted pairs at every step: True
2. The rule as sealed, order 3: what the 80 configurations are
   80 configurations: 48 tilings and 32 that are not; 16 of the 64 tilings never appear
3. The referee's exact law of K against every tiling of orders 4 and 5 (my own enumeration)
   order 4: share of the 1,024 tilings with K = 0, 1, ...: 0.125000, 0.812500, 0.062500, 0.000000; the law: 0.125000, 0.812500, 0.062500, 0.000000; largest difference 1.1e-16
   order 5: share of the 32,768 tilings with K = 0, 1, ...: 0.062500, 0.734375, 0.203125, 0.000000, 0.000000; the law: 0.062500, 0.734375, 0.203125, 0.000000, 0.000000; largest difference 2.5e-16
4. My hundred runs against the exact law
   n =   100: mean K 16.56 (exact 16.492; z = +0.6); sd 1.10 (exact 1.209); excess over the circle 1.92 blocks = 0.41 n^(1/3) (exact 0.398)
   n =   200: mean K 31.93 (exact 31.729; z = +1.3); sd 1.47 (exact 1.508); excess over the circle 2.64 blocks = 0.45 n^(1/3) (exact 0.417)
   n =   400: mean K 62.15 (exact 61.767; z = +2.0); sd 1.61 (exact 1.887); excess over the circle 3.57 blocks = 0.48 n^(1/3) (exact 0.433)
   n =   800: mean K 121.46 (exact 121.293; z = +0.7); sd 1.87 (exact 2.367); excess over the circle 4.30 blocks = 0.46 n^(1/3) (exact 0.445)
   n =  1600: mean K 239.31 (exact 239.645; z = -1.1); sd 2.96 (exact 2.974); excess over the circle 5.00 blocks = 0.43 n^(1/3) (exact 0.456)
   exponent of the sd: five sizes 0.319; without 1,600: 0.240; the exact law over the five sizes: 0.325
   correlation of K between neighbouring sizes of the same growth: 0.56, 0.58, 0.49, 0.49
5. How much is deleted at each step (one growth, read at orders 200, 400, 800)
   going to order 200: 5,308 facing pairs deleted = 0.27 of the 39,800 dominoes; fills 5,508
   going to order 400: 21,662 facing pairs deleted = 0.27 of the 159,600 dominoes; fills 22,062
   going to order 800: 86,855 facing pairs deleted = 0.27 of the 639,200 dominoes; fills 87,655
